  "published": "2026-10-14T14:52:38.983Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "DotCov 4.0.0 is built for coding agents and scripts; three contracts change.\n1. Streams: stdout carries only data; the verdict of check, test and crap is always the first stderr line, PASS included.\n2. Exit codes: a failed dotnet test run inside dotcov test exits 6 (was 5); the Fallout component exits with dotcov's codes 1-5 instead of one generic failure.\n3. JSON: every document opens with schemaVersion, command, inputs and warnings; uncoveredLines arrays become \"uncovered\" range strings; crap's gate.reason is the full verdict line.\nNew: --format json|md and --top on check and test with a gate object and worst-first offenders (uncovered ranges, partial branches); report --top; a Location column in crap; per-command --help; did-you-mean for options and commands; a warning when a directory matches no report; --no-color; diff lists only changed files; Fallout --coverage-json-path.\nFull notes: https://github.com/ANcpLua/dotcov/blob/main/docs/releases/4.0.0.md",
